<%# The Casting box of a date that has nothing to draw in it, as one quiet
    line with the one thing to press (Tim, 2026-11-18). Two cases:

      :off       casting is off for this date. It used to show no Casting
                 box at all, and the only way to turn it on was Edit,
                 Casting & Visibility.
      :no_roles  casting is on and there are no roles to cast. It used to
                 say "0/0 roles have been cast" and "No roles defined yet".

    Each sentence is checked against what's true of this date: whether
    anybody is still assigned to it, whether its roles are its own or the
    production's, and whether casting has been set up at all.

    A date with casting on keeps its way to its own casting page ("Manage
    Cast", or "View Cast" for someone who can't change it), where roles of
    its own can be added: the line adds to that, it doesn't replace it.

    Locals: show, production, kind (:off or :no_roles). %>
<%
  manager = current_user_can_manage?(production)
  what = event_type_label(show.event_type).downcase
  button = nil
  cast_page = { text: (manager ? "Manage Cast" : "View Cast"), path: manage_casting_show_cast_path(production, show), variant: "secondary" }
  if kind == :off
    cast_page = nil
    assigned = show.show_person_role_assignments.size
    text = production.casts_people? ? "Casting is off for this #{what}" : "We don't cast people in #{production.name}, so casting is off for this #{what}"
    text += if assigned.zero?
      production.casts_people? ? ", so nobody is assigned to it." : ", and nobody is assigned to it."
    else
      ". #{pluralize(assigned, 'person')} cast in it earlier #{assigned == 1 ? 'is' : 'are'} still on it."
    end
    button = { text: "Turn casting on", path: manage_turn_casting_on_show_path(production, show), method: :post, variant: "secondary" } if manager
  elsif production.casting_not_set_up?
    text = "Casting isn't set up for #{production.name} yet, so there is nothing to cast on this date."
    button = { text: "Set up casting", path: manage_casting_setup_path(production), variant: "primary" } if manager
  elsif show.use_custom_roles? || show.act_based?
    # Its roles (or its running order) are its own, and they are added on
    # the date's own casting page.
    text = show.act_based? ? "This #{what} has no acts in its running order yet, so there is nothing to cast." : "This #{what} has roles of its own, and none have been added yet, so there is nothing to cast."
    button = cast_page.merge(variant: "primary")
    cast_page = nil
  else
    text = "#{production.name} has no roles yet, so there is nothing to cast on this date."
    button = { text: "Add roles", path: manage_casting_settings_section_path(production_id: production, section: "roles"), variant: "primary" } if manager
  end
%>
<div class="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg bg-white px-4 py-3 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3" data-show-casting-note="<%= kind %>">
  <div class="min-w-0 flex-1 basis-64">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Casting</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-0.5"><%= text %></p>
  </div>
  <% if button || cast_page %>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
      <% if cast_page %><%= render "shared/button", { size: "small" }.merge(cast_page) %><% end %>
      <% if button %><%= render "shared/button", { size: "small" }.merge(button) %><% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
